(227057, 13060, 1031, '<td valign="top">This was a tricky challenge for me because so much of my thoughts about images lean towards their use in a graphic context, as most stock photos are used. I''ve posted the <a href="//www.pbase.com/image/13717605" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">original image</a> (cropped but before the color manipulation and a <a href="//www.pbase.com/image/13717669" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">cover mock-up</a> for a fictional trade magazine (frequent users of stock photos) as my image might have been used.<br/>BTW: the basic premise of the story is true (from a radio news report), but all of the details are made up.<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.pbase.com/image/13717605/small.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.pbase.com/image/13717605/small.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.pbase.com/image/13717605/small.jpg"/> <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.pbase.com/image/13717669/small.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.pbase.com/image/13717669/small.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.pbase.com/image/13717669/small.jpg"/></td>', 'This was a tricky challenge for me because so much of my thoughts about images lean towards their use in a graphic context, as most stock photos are used. I''ve posted the original image (cropped but before the color manipulation and a cover mock-up for a fictional trade magazine (frequent users of stock photos) as my image might have been used.BTW: the basic premise of the story is true (from a radio news report), but all of the details are made up. ', '2003-03-03 00:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(227062, 13087, 3575, '<td valign="top">In my haste, I put a stupid title on this photograph. It is Seattle, Washington, USA. I took it three hours before the submission deadline and just titled it its nickname, The Emerald City. I love how so many members appreciated the lighting. The sun was just about to go below the horizon in the west and this is looking east toward the city. It also helped that the usual dark, gray, dreary sky was unusually crystal clear blue. I was pleasantly surprised at the blue reflections in the windows, I didn''t expect that effect. To all of those who saw what I wanted you to see, thank you! Someone once said that timing is everything in photography.</td>', 'In my haste, I put a stupid title on this photograph. It is Seattle, Washington, USA. I took it three hours before the submission deadline and just titled it its nickname, The Emerald City. I love how so many members appreciated the lighting. The sun was just about to go below the horizon in the west and this is looking east toward the city. It also helped that the usual dark, gray, dreary sky was unusually crystal clear blue. I was pleasantly surprised at the blue reflections in the windows, I didn''t expect that effect. To all of those who saw what I wanted you to see, thank you! Someone once said that timing is everything in photography.', '2003-03-03 00:24:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(227065, 13045, 3575, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Bod, I loved this photo and I''m very glad you won.</td>', 'Congratulations Bod, I loved this photo and I''m very glad you won.', '2003-03-03 00:26:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(227129, 13045, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by autool:</b></div><hr/><i>Kentucky Fried Chicken probably wouldn''t buy this but other fanciers of the foul should love it.   It is a perfect portrait both technically and compositionally. ( Is that a word?)   10</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Fowl fanciers should like it too. Never resist a pun -- the strain is unhealthy.</td>', 'Originally posted by autool:Kentucky Fried Chicken probably wouldn''t buy this but other fanciers of the foul should love it.   It is a perfect portrait both technically and compositionally. ( Is that a word?)   10  Fowl fanciers should like it too. Never resist a pun -- the strain is unhealthy.', '2003-03-03 00:59:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(227154, 13082, 92, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your win ! This is one of the best flag photos I''ve seen in a long long time ! Just beautiful :)</td>', 'Congrats on your win ! This is one of the best flag photos I''ve seen in a long long time ! Just beautiful :)', '2003-03-03 01:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(227169, 12872, 714, '<td valign="top">Wow!!!! You got 2nd.  I didn''t think it would.  congrats!!!</td>', 'Wow!!!! You got 2nd.  I didn''t think it would.  congrats!!!', '2003-03-03 01:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(227171, 13082, 714, '<td valign="top">Congrats!!!!  Great shot!</td>', 'Congrats!!!!  Great shot!', '2003-03-03 01:32:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(227175, 13045, 714, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if I would eat chicken after looking at this. I do like the picture.  The focus is right on!  <br/> <br/>Congrats!!!!</td>', 'I don''t know if I would eat chicken after looking at this. I do like the picture.  The focus is right on!   Congrats!!!!', '2003-03-03 01:35:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(227238, 12987, 4805, '<td valign="top">great shot, but yeah, ''i see dead people''. bit of a creepy look on her face! the first thing i thought when i saw it was that it might be better if she was facing to the right...reading right to left generally works better for most of us.</td>', 'great shot, but yeah, ''i see dead people''. bit of a creepy look on her face! the first thing i thought when i saw it was that it might be better if she was facing to the right...reading right to left generally works better for most of us.', '2003-03-03 04:04:04.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(227241, 13109, 1863, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club!<br/> <br/>I liked this image a lot, and I gave it a fairly high score. I like the excellent composition, and the great shalow DOF you chose. What I think got you was the very harsh light you used, and the way the light glares off the pipe. To make it better you could have made the lovely designs on the "cup" of the pipe the focal point. IN other words move the back to the front, and do the shalow dof that way.<br/>As for whether this is meeting the challenge? I think so. It could be an advertisement for a pipe, or used for a magazine article on pipe smoking.. etc. so Challenge met :)<br/>Great work!<br/>-Annida</td>', 'Hello from the Critique club! I liked this image a lot, and I gave it a fairly high score. I like the excellent composition, and the great shalow DOF you chose. What I think got you was the very harsh light you used, and the way the light glares off the pipe. To make it better you could have made the lovely designs on the "cup" of the pipe the focal point. IN other words move the back to the front, and do the shalow dof that way.As for whether this is meeting the challenge? I think so. It could be an advertisement for a pipe, or used for a magazine article on pipe smoking.. etc. so Challenge met :)Great work!-Annida', '2003-03-03 04:14:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(227261, 13021, 2716, '<td valign="top">lol.  Much better than anticipated.  Some people saw the humor in adding the text to the image.  :)</td>', 'lol.  Much better than anticipated.  Some people saw the humor in adding the text to the image.  :)', '2003-03-03 05:43:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(227262, 12988, 1863, '<td valign="top">Hello From the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Goody for getting one of my favorites of the week! Well, let me tell you what I thought of this. I can say I absolutely loved it. It is very very simple, and very effective.  The lighting is perfect, the white isn''t too bright, and the twigs in the background are nicely in focus. I think maybe it would look better without the curvy lines at the top. It would then be a complete study of negative space, which is not what you were aiming for. This could be used for various magazines, including architecture, real estate, nature, etc. <br/>Well done!<br/>-Annida</td>', 'Hello From the Critique Club! Goody for getting one of my favorites of the week! Well, let me tell you what I thought of this. I can say I absolutely loved it. It is very very simple, and very effective.  The lighting is perfect, the white isn''t too bright, and the twigs in the background are nicely in focus. I think maybe it would look better without the curvy lines at the top. It would then be a complete study of negative space, which is not what you were aiming for. This could be used for various magazines, including architecture, real estate, nature, etc. Well done!-Annida', '2003-03-03 05:52:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(227265, 12849, 1829, '<td valign="top">At least you made the top 5, but I believe that your shot was probably the best imo.  Like you stated before:  It has that dramatic feel in which I felt as well as the viewer.  A top shot and it is certainly going in my favs.</td>', 'At least you made the top 5, but I believe that your shot was probably the best imo.  Like you stated before:  It has that dramatic feel in which I felt as well as the viewer.  A top shot and it is certainly going in my favs.', '2003-03-03 06:07:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(227291, 12872, 3326, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for your votes and, specially, who made comments.<br/>This shot initially was a glass with red wine, but first I took some shots with the empty one and the results were nicer to me. The glass was set up in front of a light box. The camera white balance was set at fluorescent light. Then some adjustments in PS (levels, contrast and a little sharp).There´s no more lighting and, of course, I used a tripod.<br/>Thanks again!<br/> <br/><a href="//www.pbase.com/pepventosa" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.pbase.com/pepventosa</a></td>', 'Thanks to all for your votes and, specially, who made comments.This shot initially was a glass with red wine, but first I took some shots with the empty one and the results were nicer to me. The glass was set up in front of a light box. The camera white balance was set at fluorescent light. Then some adjustments in PS (levels, contrast and a little sharp).There´s no more lighting and, of course, I used a tripod.Thanks again! //www.pbase.com/pepventosa', '2003-03-03 07:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(227294, 13033, 472, '<td valign="top">this pic was the coolest. totally shoulda won</td>', 'this pic was the coolest. totally shoulda won', '2003-03-03 07:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(227312, 13045, 4482, '<td valign="top">Good one Bod!  :-)</td>', 'Good one Bod!  :-)', '2003-03-03 08:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(227321, 13045, 1202, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your win and perfect entry.<br/>Autool</td>', 'Congratulations on your win and perfect entry.Autool', '2003-03-03 08:43:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(227322, 12988, 2764, '<td valign="top">This was my favorite from the challenge - I only gave one ten.  I think it faltered in the placing because it didn''t fit peoples preconcieved notion of stock.  None the less it is a beautiful photo... and yes, it is more "emotive" - a step away from your tightly controlled work.  VERY nice use of color.</td>', 'This was my favorite from the challenge - I only gave one ten.  I think it faltered in the placing because it didn''t fit peoples preconcieved notion of stock.  None the less it is a beautiful photo... and yes, it is more "emotive" - a step away from your tightly controlled work.  VERY nice use of color.', '2003-03-03 08:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(227327, 13096, 2764, '<td valign="top">Grrr - what is this doing way down here?  Now I feel badly that I only gave you a nine - I subtracted a point for the light swtitch.  This is a waaay under reated photo.  Probaby it is in the wrong challenge, maybe people couldn''t see stock possibilites/</td>', 'Grrr - what is this doing way down here?  Now I feel badly that I only gave you a nine - I subtracted a point for the light swtitch.  This is a waaay under reated photo.  Probaby it is in the wrong challenge, maybe people couldn''t see stock possibilites/', '2003-03-03 09:00:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(227360, 13041, 3102, '<td valign="top">Dang -- looks like I''ll be eating shoe!  I still insist that this should have been a top 3 -- excellent work!</td>', 'Dang -- looks like I''ll be eating shoe!  I still insist that this should have been a top 3 -- excellent work!', '2003-03-03 09:39:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(227363, 13041, 4162, '<td valign="top">I too thought that this would get the big one! Great shot!</td>', 'I too thought that this would get the big one! Great shot!', '2003-03-03 09:41:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(227431, 12812, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>Out of focus. A little bland.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content/ Background </b> <br/>Youve already mentioned focus in your own comments, so I am not telling you anything new when I say this image suffers from lack of sharp focus.<br/>I do like the jewellery itself though Id not know without you telling me that a) its jewellery as opposed to a fancy bottle tag and b) that its the main focus of the image.<br/>Aspects I find offputting: the bottle does not seem to be entirely vertical within the image; the background would be better curved beneath the bottle to create a seamless background to the image; the colour of the background clashes with the two colours in the bottle; the composition is a little unbalanced  too close to centred to be successful as a non-centred composition but too far from centred to work as a centred composition; because the background is so busy I find the shadow on the background more interesting than the foreground object itself.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Focus, as above.<br/>Might be worth playing with lighting  how about secondary lighting through the bottle from behind, what about softer lighting or perhaps harsher lighting providing some highlights off the bottle and jewellery?<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Not hugely, for me. I think that this would be the kind of thing which a jeweller might commission but would make little sense as a generic addition to a stock library  the jewellery is too prominent for it to be used as a generic bottle of perfume or alcohol.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>Would love to see this retaken with some changes as discussed above.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club   Initial thoughts Out of focus. A little bland. Composition/ Content/ Background  Youve already mentioned focus in your own comments, so I am not telling you anything new when I say this image suffers from lack of sharp focus.I do like the jewellery itself though Id not know without you telling me that a) its jewellery as opposed to a fancy bottle tag and b) that its the main focus of the image.Aspects I find offputting: the bottle does not seem to be entirely vertical within the image; the background would be better curved beneath the bottle to create a seamless background to the image; the colour of the background clashes with the two colours in the bottle; the composition is a little unbalanced  too close to centred to be successful as a non-centred composition but too far from centred to work as a centred composition; because the background is so busy I find the shadow on the background more interesting than the foreground object itself. Camera Work - Technical Focus, as above.Might be worth playing with lighting  how about secondary lighting through the bottle from behind, what about softer lighting or perhaps harsher lighting providing some highlights off the bottle and jewellery? Fits The Challenge Not hugely, for me. I think that this would be the kind of thing which a jeweller might commission but would make little sense as a generic addition to a stock library  the jewellery is too prominent for it to be used as a generic bottle of perfume or alcohol. My Opinion On The Photo Would love to see this retaken with some changes as discussed above.', '2003-03-03 10:28:30.000000', NULL, 0),
