(227874, 13110, 1360, '<td valign="top">I like the background colors, and how the cactus reaches diagonally out.  I think i''d prefer this if it was cropped above the horizon though, and just show sky.</td>', 'I like the background colors, and how the cactus reaches diagonally out.  I think i''d prefer this if it was cropped above the horizon though, and just show sky.', '2003-03-03 16:39:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(228004, 13071, 1280, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comments by Grayce<br/>I like this very much. Pine cones always appeal to me and you did a nice job capturing this image.  <br/>The composition is good, and it''s nice you didn''t center the pine cones. The way you cropped works well, that you included some pine needles in focus and the diagonal branches leading the eye to the cones.<br/>It''s a simple picture, which adds to the appeal.  The little bit of green makes it fresh and refreshing. There is a hint of texture on the branches.  That''s nice.<br/>There is nothing I don''t like here, except maybe brighten the pine cones a little, but it is acceptable.  So what more can I say?  Good job!<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce</td>', 'Critique Club Comments by GrayceI like this very much. Pine cones always appeal to me and you did a nice job capturing this image.  The composition is good, and it''s nice you didn''t center the pine cones. The way you cropped works well, that you included some pine needles in focus and the diagonal branches leading the eye to the cones.It''s a simple picture, which adds to the appeal.  The little bit of green makes it fresh and refreshing. There is a hint of texture on the branches.  That''s nice.There is nothing I don''t like here, except maybe brighten the pine cones a little, but it is acceptable.  So what more can I say?  Good job!Regards, Grayce', '2003-03-03 17:49:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(228006, 13061, 3607, '<td valign="top">1) i can see now that this is more of a photojournalistic photo than a stock photo, and what a stock photo should be is clearer to me now than before.<br/>2) i think there is ''grade-inflation'' in the members only voting arena, because i thought my ''honeymoon hell'' photo was much better than this one.  that said, my honeymoon hell photo was placed in the middle of the pack while this one placed very much in the end . . .<br/> <br/>thanks for all your comments.</td>', '1) i can see now that this is more of a photojournalistic photo than a stock photo, and what a stock photo should be is clearer to me now than before.2) i think there is ''grade-inflation'' in the members only voting arena, because i thought my ''honeymoon hell'' photo was much better than this one.  that said, my honeymoon hell photo was placed in the middle of the pack while this one placed very much in the end . . . thanks for all your comments.', '2003-03-03 17:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(228010, 12888, 715, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes and comments.<br/>I''m not a stock-photographer so I didn''t even think about the disturbing factor of the text on the bulb. I can see it now though, so thanks for pointing it out.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the votes and comments.I''m not a stock-photographer so I didn''t even think about the disturbing factor of the text on the bulb. I can see it now though, so thanks for pointing it out. ', '2003-03-03 17:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(228041, 13000, 6711, '<td valign="top">Your 6th place is not enough to me. Your submission was the best of the week in my opinion (though is only one''s oppinion). Is a very good shot (colour, composition, light...) and also has a lot to communicate. For exemple, about today''s break in the world?.Meets perfectly the challenge.<br/>DPC is very good in a lot of ways. One way is because we can see pictures like yours. But in other ways, is a little bit dissapoinment with some results. Although, that''s the real life. Isn''t?.<br/> Keep on rockin!</td>', 'Your 6th place is not enough to me. Your submission was the best of the week in my opinion (though is only one''s oppinion). Is a very good shot (colour, composition, light...) and also has a lot to communicate. For exemple, about today''s break in the world?.Meets perfectly the challenge.DPC is very good in a lot of ways. One way is because we can see pictures like yours. But in other ways, is a little bit dissapoinment with some results. Although, that''s the real life. Isn''t?. Keep on rockin!', '2003-03-03 18:34:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(228076, 12904, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> Hello teachme53 <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes.<br/>Composition-Lovely <br/>Background-N/A <br/>My Opinion-The pose, the girl, the light is so wonderful here....butterscotch cream. The focus is the only negative that I can possible pick at. &lt;lol&gt; I like this, I like here, the shot! Good work. Hope you''ll try a tripod if you didn''t. This is nice work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'CC Hello teachme53 Fits The Challenge-Yes.Composition-Lovely Background-N/A My Opinion-The pose, the girl, the light is so wonderful here....butterscotch cream. The focus is the only negative that I can possible pick at. <lol> I like this, I like here, the shot! Good work. Hope you''ll try a tripod if you didn''t. This is nice work. ', '2003-03-03 18:54:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(228091, 13096, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC club!<br/> <br/>As a fellow Coolpix 4500 it''s a nice shot.<br/> <br/>THEME: I think the picture does meet the challenge but in my opinion stock photography should represent and focus on 1 object and here we have a flower and a lamp. I don''t even see a link between the two objects... a common theme.<br/> <br/>FOCUS and LIGHTING: Good focus and lighting. I think that the graininess (especially in the lamp shade)in the pic is due to the color over-saturation.<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: The cropping is good and the shadows on the wall gives depth to the photo. The pink is too bright for me but that''s a personal statement. :-)  But I do think that going on the edge with the color would limit the sell of your pic in a stock catalogue as most people look for something more common.<br/> <br/>Good luck and have fun!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC club! As a fellow Coolpix 4500 it''s a nice shot. THEME: I think the picture does meet the challenge but in my opinion stock photography should represent and focus on 1 object and here we have a flower and a lamp. I don''t even see a link between the two objects... a common theme. FOCUS and LIGHTING: Good focus and lighting. I think that the graininess (especially in the lamp shade)in the pic is due to the color over-saturation. COMPOSITION: The cropping is good and the shadows on the wall gives depth to the photo. The pink is too bright for me but that''s a personal statement. :-)  But I do think that going on the edge with the color would limit the sell of your pic in a stock catalogue as most people look for something more common. Good luck and have fun!', '2003-03-03 19:13:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(228096, 13005, 4482, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC club!<br/> <br/>THEME: Met! A nice little niche.<br/> <br/>LIGHTING and FOCUS: The lights and darks are well balanced and the focus is where it should be.<br/> <br/>CROPPING: Well done.<br/> <br/>COMPOSITION: I think that having a "happy" military man ruins the atmosphere of the pic. I don''t think it represents the military life at all.. especially not for stock. It''s also very static which is an oposite image of the military. The photo seems to be missing some "UMPF" to make it really work.<br/> <br/>All the best!<br/> <br/>Have fun!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC club! THEME: Met! A nice little niche. LIGHTING and FOCUS: The lights and darks are well balanced and the focus is where it should be. CROPPING: Well done. COMPOSITION: I think that having a "happy" military man ruins the atmosphere of the pic. I don''t think it represents the military life at all.. especially not for stock. It''s also very static which is an oposite image of the military. The photo seems to be missing some "UMPF" to make it really work. All the best! Have fun!', '2003-03-03 19:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(228207, 12987, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> Evening crabappl3 <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-YES <br/>Composition-Perfect light, chair, bow, young girl. <br/>Background-Good, yes, I guess a drape would of been better, but I do like the wall. I like the lighting on her hair, but agree the pillow could go. Still I understand &lt;hard chair&gt;! <br/>My Opinion-Nice photo of a darling young lady doing a good job. SHE is perfect for this ''stock'' shot. Your b&amp;w tones are extremely nice.<br/> <br/></td>', 'CC Evening crabappl3  Fits The Challenge-YES Composition-Perfect light, chair, bow, young girl. Background-Good, yes, I guess a drape would of been better, but I do like the wall. I like the lighting on her hair, but agree the pillow could go. Still I understand <hard chair>! My Opinion-Nice photo of a darling young lady doing a good job. SHE is perfect for this ''stock'' shot. Your b&w tones are extremely nice. ', '2003-03-03 20:50:57.000000', NULL, 0),
